title: ToadArea01Dialogue
---
Sir Thomas Toad: Oh, hello! Guess you could understand me after all.

Sir Thomas Toad: Either that or you just followed me, but I am choosing to believe in your capabilities.

Green Soul: …

Sir Thomas Toad: Anyhow, fascinating is it not?

Sir Thomas Toad: Remnants of the past like these never fail to impress me.

Sir Thomas Toad: Even a door like this can tell us so much about how the people who inhabited these ruins lived.

Sir Thomas Toad: I wish I could somehow talk to someone from that time. I would have so much to ask…

//(Green Soul suddenly hears whispers from the depths of the ruins)

Desert Soul: …oul…atch…rpos…eal…

Desert Soul: Derelict soul… The profaned egg will soon hatch… Fulfill your purpose… Reapply the seal…

Sir Thomas Toad: …ou okay?

Green Soul: …!

Sir Thomas Toad: Can you hear me now? Your gaze was fixated on the passage downward.

Green Soul: …

//(Green Soul goes in the direction of the tunnels leading down)

Sir Thomas Toad: Are you proceeding deeper into the ruins? You should be careful, there are some rather fierce beasts roaming the tunnels.
Sir Thomas Toad: I would follow you to help, but I am well past my fighting days…

//(Green Soul walks a bit more)

Sir Thomas Toad: Wait, before you leave, I have a small request.

Sir Thomas Toad: I know I am in no position to ask for favors, as we have just met.

Sir Thomas Toad: But if you by any chance run into MATERIALS NAMES, would you be so kind as to bring them back to the area where we met earlier?

Sir Thomas Toad: I am thinking of establishing myself around the ruins to study them in more depth, so these materials would help me make a small base of operations.

Sir Thomas Toad: And do not worry, I will make sure to reward you well if you do choose to help.

Sir Thomas Toad: Well then, do not let me hold you any longer.

Sir Thomas Toad: Best of luck down there!

<<enable_movement ToadDialogueTrigger>>

===
